body:
How embarrassing!
Crying in front of passers-by.

And wonder what you saw that moved you,
what you heard, what they did to you.
Throw their prying eyes at you

watching you wrestle with your tears and your nose;

to listen, with their prying ears, to the spasms of your muscles;

smell, with their prying nose, the primitive smell of crying;

not to know that you are crying for love
not to know that you are crying from love

because
they will not have read, with their prying eyes,
the most beautiful letters in the world;

they will not have heard, with their prying ears,
the most honest thing I miss about you in the world;

they will not have smelled, with their prying nose,
the most sacred body in the world;

so they don't cry.

What a shame they will feel!

85 — m
